0..74 Comment "//! The two checks of `boot-core` over `Ptr.Eff`: whether a range is valid"
75..150 Comment "//! UTF-8, and where its first zero byte is, the byte that ends a C string."
151..154 Comment "//!"
155..229 Comment "//! `check_utf8` and `find_zero` give the answers of the Rust functions of"
230..306 Comment "//! `crates/boot-core/src/check.rs`. They name no model of memory: the scope"
307..381 Comment "//! that handles `Ptr.Eff` chooses one. Each reads one byte at a time with"
382..459 Comment "//! `load8`, and it reads a byte only when the range holds it. An empty range"
460..535 Comment "//! can have any address, and no check reads it. Each check descends on the"
536..586 Comment "//! length of its range, as `ranges.gandr` states."
587..590 Comment "//!"
591..668 Comment "//! The check of UTF-8 follows the table of well-formed byte sequences of the"
669..722 Comment "//! Unicode standard, as `core::str::from_utf8` does:"
723..726 Comment "//!"
727..775 Comment "//! - A lead byte below 128 is a whole sequence."
776..853 Comment "//! - A lead byte from 194 to 223 starts a sequence of two bytes, from 224 to"
854..931 Comment "//!   239 one of three, and from 240 to 244 one of four. Each other lead byte"
932..949 Comment "//!   is a fault."
950..1027 Comment "//! - A continuation byte is from 128 to 191. The second byte after the leads"
1028..1077 Comment "//!   224, 237, 240 and 244 has a narrower range."
1078..1156 Comment "//! - A fault is at the position of the lead byte of its sequence, and so is a"
1157..1192 Comment "//!   sequence that the range cuts."
1193..1196 Comment "//!"
1197..1274 Comment "//! The `runs` items run the cases of `crates/boot-core/tests/check.rs` under"
1275..1353 Comment "//! `Extent`. Each range ends at the end of the extent, so a read past it ends"
1354..1381 Comment "//! the run with `Outside`."
1382..1385 Comment "//!"
1386..1445 Comment "//! - see: `ranges.gandr` — `Range`, `Length` and `Found`"
1446..1512 Comment "//! - see: `search.gandr` — `find_byte`, which `find_zero` calls"
1513..1587 Comment "//! - see: `../../../library/std/src/ptr.gandr` — `Ptr.Eff` and `Extent`"
1588..1662 Comment "//! - see: `../../../crates/boot-core/src/check.rs` — the Rust functions"
